    "notes": {
        "2af4c245-c5a0-478b-8a59-fcf1d073d497": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 336,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 320,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Instance-specific URL, and what this flow can NOT cover\n\n**`apiBaseUrl` in SetVariable must be the API URL of the instance this flow runs on** (`appmixer url`), e.g. `https://api-dev-automated-00001.dev.appmixer.ai`. Plugin routes are only reachable on the tenant's own API host, and the `resource` value the endpoint reports comes from `MCP_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` / `APPMIXER_API_URL` on the backend — a mismatch is exactly what this flow is meant to catch.\n\nThe authenticated half of the endpoint (`POST /mcp` JSON-RPC: `initialize`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`; the `GET /mcp` SSE stream) is **deliberately not tested here**: it needs a user bearer token, and no token may be committed to this repo. The 401 + `WWW-Authenticate` challenge and the `DELETE /mcp` → 405 contract are also out of reach, because `appmixer.utils.http.*` throws on any non-2xx response and would stop the flow.\n\nThose paths are covered by `test/ai/mcptools/{mcp-auth,streamable-http}.test.js` and, against a live instance, by `src/appmixer/ai/mcptools/artifacts/mcp-server-simulation/run-e2e-test.sh`."
        }
    }
